Subject: [PATCH] launch_daemon: throttle service respawns

B_SYSTEM_OBJECT_UPDATE's B_TEAM_DELETED handler relaunched a `service`
job the instant its team died, with a `// TODO: take restart throttle
into account` left right above the call -- a gap Haiku's own
launch_daemon authors already knew about, just never closed.

With virtio-net-pci attached under QEMU/hvf (this port's own test
environment; not reproduced with no network device present), one or
more of the "legacy" services declared in data/launch/system -- media_server
and sshd, observed independently of each other -- can exit immediately
after every launch attempt for reasons that have nothing to do with
this TODO (that root cause is still open: see AGENTS.md). Without a
minimum interval between attempts, launch_daemon's own team-deletion
handler relaunches the job as fast as the kernel can create and tear
down a team: confirmed via a kernel thread dump showing the job's team
ID climbing by ~3000 every 5 seconds with the resident team/thread/
semaphore/port counts and free memory all staying flat (no leak --
every attempt is cleaned up, just immediately replaced by the next
one). That respawn storm saturates the CPU in process-creation
overhead alone and starves the rest of boot of any time to run,
independent of whatever made the first launch fail.

This gives each Job a timestamp of its last launch attempt (Job::Launch(),
read back via the new Job::LastLaunchTime()) and, when a service's team
dies less than a second after that timestamp, defers the relaunch with
a one-shot BMessageRunner instead of calling _LaunchJob() immediately.
A service that fails once still recovers within about a second, same as
before; one that fails repeatedly now retries at roughly 1 Hz instead of
in a tight loop.

This is upstream launch_daemon code (src/servers/launch/), not something
this port's own patches otherwise touch -- confirmed, well-contained fix
regardless of what turns out to be causing the underlying respawn in the
first place, worth upstreaming.

diff --git a/src/servers/launch/Job.cpp b/src/servers/launch/Job.cpp
index b696c48674..3b46ec20e1 100644
--- a/src/servers/launch/Job.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/launch/Job.cpp
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@ Job::Job(const char* name)
 	fLaunching(false),
 	fInitStatus(B_NO_INIT),
 	fTeam(-1),
+	fLastLaunchTime(0),
 	fDefaultPort(-1),
 	fToken((uint32)B_PREFERRED_TOKEN),
 	fLaunchStatus(B_NO_INIT),
@@ -50,6 +51,7 @@ Job::Job(const Job& other)
 	fLaunching(other.IsLaunching()),
 	fInitStatus(B_NO_INIT),
 	fTeam(-1),
+	fLastLaunchTime(0),
 	fDefaultPort(-1),
 	fToken((uint32)B_PREFERRED_TOKEN),
 	fLaunchStatus(B_NO_INIT),
@@ -306,6 +308,13 @@ Job::Team() const
 }


+bigtime_t
+Job::LastLaunchTime() const
+{
+	return fLastLaunchTime;
+}
+
+
 const PortMap&
 Job::Ports() const
 {
@@ -351,6 +360,8 @@ Job::SetDefaultPort(port_id port)
 status_t
 Job::Launch()
 {
+	fLastLaunchTime = system_time();
+
 	// Build environment

 	std::vector<const char*> environment;
diff --git a/src/servers/launch/Job.h b/src/servers/launch/Job.h
index aac20fcae5..7a5cfd602f 100644
--- a/src/servers/launch/Job.h
+++ b/src/servers/launch/Job.h
@@ -81,6 +81,8 @@ public:

 			team_id				Team() const;

+			bigtime_t			LastLaunchTime() const;
+
 			const PortMap&		Ports() const;
 			port_id				Port(const char* name = NULL) const;

@@ -134,6 +136,7 @@ private:
 			PortMap				fPortMap;
 			status_t			fInitStatus;
 			team_id				fTeam;
+			bigtime_t			fLastLaunchTime;
 			port_id				fDefaultPort;
 			uint32				fToken;
 			status_t			fLaunchStatus;
diff --git a/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.cpp b/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.cpp
index 5e30134bde..33ee3e56d1 100644
--- a/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.cpp
+++ b/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.cpp
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
 #include <driver_settings.h>
 #include <Entry.h>
 #include <File.h>
+#include <MessageRunner.h>
 #include <ObjectList.h>
 #include <Path.h>
 #include <PathFinder.h>
@@ -587,8 +588,26 @@ LaunchDaemon::MessageReceived(BMessage* message)
 					status_t status = rosterPrivate.IsShutDownInProgress(
 						&inProgress);
 					if (status != B_OK || !inProgress) {
-						// TODO: take restart throttle into account
-						_LaunchJob(job);
+						// Services that exit again right after being
+						// launched (for example because something they
+						// depend on, like a network link, isn't ready yet)
+						// must not be relaunched as fast as the system can
+						// manage: with no minimum interval between
+						// attempts, a service stuck failing on every
+						// launch starves the rest of the system of CPU
+						// time in a tight respawn loop instead of a few
+						// retries a second.
+						static const bigtime_t kMinRestartInterval = 1000000;
+						bigtime_t elapsed
+							= system_time() - job->LastLaunchTime();
+						if (elapsed >= kMinRestartInterval) {
+							_LaunchJob(job);
+						} else {
+							BMessage restart(kMsgRestartJob);
+							restart.AddString("name", job->Name());
+							BMessageRunner::StartSending(BMessenger(this),
+								&restart, kMinRestartInterval - elapsed, 1);
+						}
 					}
 				}
 			}
@@ -687,6 +706,20 @@ LaunchDaemon::MessageReceived(BMessage* message)
 			_HandleGetLaunchLog(message);
 			break;

+		case kMsgRestartJob:
+		{
+			// A throttled service restart (see B_SYSTEM_OBJECT_UPDATE
+			// above) is now due.
+			const char* name = message->GetString("name");
+			if (name == NULL)
+				break;
+
+			Job* job = FindJob(name);
+			if (job != NULL && !job->IsRunning())
+				_LaunchJob(job);
+			break;
+		}
+
 		case kMsgEventTriggered:
 		{
 			// An internal event has been triggered.
diff --git a/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.h b/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.h
index ace8a9fbbc..44e153d654 100644
--- a/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.h
+++ b/src/servers/launch/LaunchDaemon.h
@@ -10,6 +10,7 @@


 static const uint32 kMsgEventTriggered = 'ldet';
+static const uint32 kMsgRestartJob = 'ldrj';


 #endif // LAUNCH_DAEMON_H
